※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4529

※ An argument that does not name its parameter is for the parameter in the
※ place it stands, and once an argument has named one the places no longer
※ count from anywhere.  So the ones written by place come first and the ones
※ written by name after, which is the order they read in anyway.  Python
※ states the same rule about the same two kinds of argument.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = plus(.n ← 2u8, 1u8)
    0u6

fn plus(n: u8, by: u8 ← 1u8) → u8:
    n + by
